aces as at baseline, with the backup key restricted to node2's address.","evidence_ids":["cmd-92cae39b349d4289","cmd-2d66cdb6cab044f2","cmd-cffefeeaf4d14012","cmd-ead2bfd3c51145bd","cmd-0b61a20521084235","cmd-71bab1a1814a422b","cmd-1e5df5eb688748bb","cmd-c69a273e59fa4a5e","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node2:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied. The provider-wide restart protocol was also complete for both nodes: each had a healthy pre-restart state, acknowledged restart, changed boot identity independently corroborated by lifecycle snapshots, and recovered system, service, credentials, and archive state.","limitations":["No unattended execution at the scheduled 02:00 time was captured; scheduling is established by the active timer, while actual transfer behavior was demonstrated through immediate service starts.","The source directory was absent initially and therefore created empty. The captured archive contains the data directory but no application files, so preservation of a representative nonempty payload was not demonstrated."]}
